I'm currently playing a samurai who has had the misfortune to go blind. 
Thankfully he ate a floating eye corpse so he's not in that bad of a 
situation because he can detect most of his adversaries.
I noticed something strange about being blind. He killed a woodland elf and 
while looting the area where the elf died he found a faded pall. Wouldn't 
knowing something is faded involve eyesight? How would a blind person know 
something is faded?
Secondly while blindly stumbling around the dungeons of doom I happened to 
find a gemstone. On my display the gemstone was violet or purple, out of 
curiousity I named it "purple" and when my sight had returned lo and behold 
the gem was a violet one! How could a blind person have guessed its hue?
This is really minor but I find this to be intriguing.

